{{Top|legends=Hover Pod}}
[[File:TheChildPod-Fathead.png|thumb|right|250px|Grogu in his first hover pram]]
A '''hover pram''', or '''hover-pram''', was a hovering device used for transporting, providing protection and shielding [[youngling]]s. The device was a valuable tool for guardians with children too young to protect themselves.<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|hovering-pram|hovering pram}}</ref>

The [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] found [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] inside a pram on [[Arvala-7]].<ref name="Chapter 1">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 1: The Mandalorian}}</ref> When Grogu was attacked, first by bounty hunters and later by a [[Mudhorn]], Djarin was able to move the pram remotely to protect him.<ref name="Chapter 2">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 2: The Child}}</ref> Djarin continued to use it to transport Grogu until handing him over to [[the Client]]. When Djarin returned to rescue Grogu, he found the capsule discarded in a dumpster.<ref name="Chapter 3">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 3: The Sin}}</ref> Then decided to use it.

Returning to Arvala-7 to recruit [[Kuiil]], Djarin used a [[hovercrate]] to transport the child. On board the ''[[Razor Crest]]'', Djarin asked Kuiil to pad the container so Grogu could sleep better, but the [[Ugnaught]] offered instead to fabricate a better hovering pram himself. Kuiil's version retained the egg shape and closing cover of Grogu's original capsule, but was fashioned out of metal.<ref name="Chapter 7">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 7: The Reckoning}}</ref> Djarin used Kuiil's capsule to transport Grogu until it was ripped open by [[Koska Reeves]] so she could retrieve Grogu after saving him from a [[mamacore]].<ref name="Chapter 11">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 11: The Heiress}}</ref>

Sometimes after, Grogu received a new spherical pram, and used it while visiting [[High Magistrate]] [[Greef Karga]] on [[Nevarro]].<ref name="Chapter 17">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 17: The Apostate}}</ref>

{{Tech-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Mandalorian_pram_sketch.png|thumb|left|250px|The first sketch of a hovering pram]]
A pram first appeared in the [[Chapter 1: The Mandalorian|first episode]] of the [[2019]] [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'', which aired on [[November 12]], 2019, and was directed by [[Dave Filoni]].<ref name="Chapter 1" /> After Filoni met [[Jon Favreau]], the creator of the show, he was trying to figure out interesting moments for the pitch of the series. While being on a plane he sketched the first drawing of the pram, which featured Grogu inside a pram with a floating ball and the Mandalorian looking at him. According to Filoni, that drawing sold the idea of the show. Concept art of the pram was later created by [[Christian Alzmann]], [[Doug Chiang]] and [[Ryan Church]]. The designers also considered keeping Grogu in a big hood instead, thinking that kids covered in big clothes look cuter, but they couldn't keep his ears in the hood. They also thought about making the pram a backpack to copy the effect of the hood, but decided against it, as they wanted the ''[[Wikipedia:Lone Wolf and Cub|Lone Wolf and Cub]]'' quality of the pram.<ref name="Art of">[[The Art of Star Wars: The Mandalorian (Season One)|''The Art of Star Wars: The Mandalorian'' Season One]]</ref>

